    "updated_at": "2026-03-11T01:52:47Z",
    "body": "As someone trying to implement the current resumable uploads draft, I would personally prefer a general means to access multiple (1xx) responses from the Fetch API rather than abstracting a built-in browser implementation of resumable uploads. That would allow for a variety of upload strategies, because there are multiple ways to implement a compliant resumable upload client with different trade-offs.\n\nFurthermore, it would just be nice to have the ability to use interim responses for use cases outside of resumable uploads, such as `Expect: 100-continue` (which probably should then change to be allowed).\n\nShould I open a new issue for that more general suggestion?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
